    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d834">

                <pb facs="0824" n="720" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg720"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6245.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-18T14:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 18, 1913—2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. Madero has just been made prisoner by Blanquette, apparently with the
                    approval of Huerta. My messenger states that the President resisted, that a
                    number of officers in the room were killed, and that he [Blanquette] afterwards
                    took a squad of men and captured Gustavo Madero in the Gambrinus restaurant.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
